  },
  {
   "post_type": "comment",
   "post_id": 7512613,
   "parent_id": 6406411,
   "parent_type": "answer",
   "author_user_id": 14065,
   "author_display_name": "Loki Astari",
   "author_id_missing": false,
   "role": "responder",
   "is_accepted": null,
   "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/6406356/#comment7512613_6406411",
   "score": 3,
   "created_utc": "2011-06-20T03:31:52Z",
   "edited": false,
   "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
   "body_html": "You should be careful using a string as the example. As the converse for loading a vector of strings is different (it is the only standard type where output/input will be different)."
  },
  {
   "post_type": "answer",
   "post_id": 39746650,
   "parent_id": 6406356,
   "author_user_id": 1298196,
   "author_display_name": "Phlox Midas",
   "author_id_missing": false,
   "role": "responder",
   "is_accepted": false,
   "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/a/39746650",
   "score": 32,
   "created_utc": "2016-09-28T11:50:48Z",
   "last_edit_utc": "2018-09-03T12:34:11Z",
   "last_activity_utc": "2018-09-03T12:34:11Z",
   "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
   "body_html": "<p>Assuming you have C++11:</p>\n\n<pre><code>#include &lt;fstream&gt;\n#include &lt;vector&gt;\n#include &lt;string&gt;\n\nint main()\n{\n    std::vector&lt;std::string&gt; v{ \"one\", \"two\", \"three\" };\n    std::ofstream outFile(\"my_file.txt\");\n    // the important part\n    for (const auto &amp;e : v) outFile &lt;&lt; e &lt;&lt; \"\\n\";\n}\n</code></pre>\n"
  },
  {
